WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.440
An ancient Hindu scripture
asks: what lets your eye see,

2
00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:06.310
and your mind think?

3
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.400
Its answer is strange.

4
00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:12.720
There the eye does not
go, nor speech, nor mind.

5
00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:17.500
Yet in temples and homes, Hindus
bathe and dress a sacred murti,

6
00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.320
and offer it food.

7
00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:22.840
So how can Hindus say
God is beyond every word,

8
00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:26.580
and also worship God
with flowers in a temple?

9
00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:30.240
In this mission, you'll meet
two ways of seeing Brahman:

10
00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:32.830
without qualities, and with them.

11
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:35.520
Then you'll find out
why one short syllable,

12
00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:38.840
Om, is said to stand for Brahman.

13
00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:43.490
Your mission: find out how Hindus
can say God is beyond words,

14
00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:45.480
yet worship God in a temple.
